    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **66 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field for created owners, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern. The warning is `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the capacity limit of 50); the hard 409 rejection at 50 (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`) is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`AssignCapacityWarning.java`** (new function class) \u2014 counts existing owners in the city case-insensitively over `findAll()` (same matching as the capacity check), running before save so the new owner is excluded, and sets `capacityWarning = 40 \u2264 inCity \u2264 49`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignCapacityWarning` step into the pipeline (after `assignBulkSignupWarning`, before `assignPossibleDuplicate`), governed by the same transaction.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` `Boolean` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean under the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps the same-named property (no explicit mapper change needed).\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column so persistence/read-back works across all DBs.\n\nThe `Cp54Tests` warning test and the `Cp18Tests` hard-limit test both pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
